    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Nurses and midwives work on the frontlines to provide healthcare. This means they hardly get time to grow their careers or catch up on the latest innovations or trends in healthcare. According to  a report by IPSOS Mori , 44% of nurses and midwives find it challenging to commit time to pursue professional development. Those working in community settings, public health facilities and in secondary care, struggle to fit Continuous Professional Development (CPD) courses in their schedules. They frequently work past their shift due to understaffing and have to see an overwhelming number of patients, leaving little time to focus on their professional development.",
